<title>GERMANY: Hamburg Airlines adds Ireland, Portugal, Greece flights.</title>
<headline>Hamburg Airlines adds Ireland, Portugal, Greece flights.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German regional carrier Hamburg Airlines said it will add new flights to Ireland, Portugal and Greece from March 30.</p>
<p>The private airline will operate four flights a week to Dublin and two services a week to Athens and Porto from Hamburg with BAE-146 aircraft.</p>
<p>Hamburg Airlines also flies four times a week to Riga, three times a week to Poznan in Poland and has several domestic German services.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
